{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 4"},"body":"Pinned source statements support the following navigation links.\n\nInspected: Configured challenge assertions, their relevant definitions and the cited audited paper statements were compared.","content_sha256":"sha256:45e337dacc3ad33fd6a2dbdb90b6b7e6a2edc316dc321ffe1a90e74976cd91a1","fingerprint":"sha256:b93a6aa353407022974b7eaaa716e87412694fdba6e0fb34b9e5521e8819f214","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. Pinned source statements support the following navigation links.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:cd20c3a47cffa87359dade3ab4d69b625a5c15aa8d0c070932c968442e250b70","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.HardSphere.condensation_with_mixed"],"explanation":"The first formal conjunct asserts an absolute positive lower limit for zero-momentum occupation along every thermodynamic sequence at positive density with rho*a^3 below an absolute threshold. Its ground vectors are normalized complex bosonic energy minimizers in the hard-sphere Dirichlet domain. This is the pure-state main theorem; the formal declaration also has a separate density-operator conjunct.","fingerprint":"sha256:1676b93b2973bbd5b6172939502e4c5f898f2befea16913f5270613e773977a2","limitations":"The Sobolev closure model and occupation normalization were inspected, but equivalence of the formal functional-analytic realization and paper Hamiltonian is not proof-certified.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Ground-state-condensation-in-the-dilute-hard-sphere-gas-September-24-2026#main:theorem","statement_sha256":"sha256:b58fd45ee167a963c557c7e83d17cba85e6dba16a7fd5e718f0490b5f74e1746"},{"declarations":["OAI.HardSphere.condensation_with_mixed"],"explanation":"The second formal conjunct gives the same positive lower limit for every density operator supported on the ground space along the stated dilute thermodynamic sequences. That is the general mixed-state conclusion of the paper corollary. Its explicit examples of normalized ground-space projections and nonnegative ground functions are not separately asserted in this conjunct.","fingerprint":"sha256:7d18e02ebdedea28cdf8b7d5d383a49710077b657bef1a364a9bbf4fd6d47967","limitations":"This is an agent source reading, not a proof replay or independently reviewed equivalence.","relation":"formal-is-part","row_id":"Ground-state-condensation-in-the-dilute-hard-sphere-gas-September-24-2026#main:mixed","statement_sha256":"sha256:2e7aa131ebbb214087cf278c033062a23bd1fc17eada13872c3a22107935b114"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/HardSphere.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Ground-state-condensation-in-the-dilute-hard-sphere-gas-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L48","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Ground-state-condensation-in-the-dilute-hard-sphere-gas-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L69"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:HardSphere","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/e5e51a3ba5089cafb7eb0e92.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/e5e51a3ba5089cafb7eb0e92.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/e5e51a3ba5089cafb7eb0e92.json","point